lfies in a second basically it's  not gonna matter at all  so either way I don't think this makes a  difference now let's talk about two  separate features one of which is on  either one of these phones that both are  great and I wish both phones had this  but it's gonna be up to you to choose  which one is more  on the 1 plus 7 Pro I absolutely love  the physical mute and vibrate switch you  can feel it even if it's in your pocket  you can click it up to get like a silent  mode or a vibrate mode and no vibrates  so without having to look at it you can  know in which mode it's in and actually  be able to change it now on the note 10  plus we do not have that you just have  your little volume rocker but one  feature we do have is the always-on  display which I love and from the  factory you cannot have that on the 1 +  7 Pro unless you do some aftermarket  stuff so this is great when the phone is  sitting on your desk when it's wireless  charging which we'll talk about in just  a second being able to see the time the  date your battery percentage different  notifications that you may have missed  is very very handy now let's talk about  something that is absolutely brilliant  with a 1 + 7 Pro and that is the  software the software that isn't here is  not sake Android it is slightly modified  but it is better than even the software  that comes on the pixel it is fluid it  is fast it is just incredible  I love the stuff they added to it I love  the menus the launcher it is really  great the keyboard that comes with it  absolutely brilliant whereas on the note  10 the one UI is ok it's better than  before but it do still get some an  occasional kind of glitches some UI  stutters some of the software stuff  doesn't make sense I don't love the  icons so if you care about great  software go for the 1 + 7 Pro if that's  your priority it is amazing  speaking about brilliant software let me  tell you about our sponsor for this  video brilliant brilliant helps you to  excel in