u have it in the auto mode which  makes it much more viewable outside  compared to the 1 plus 7 Pro now both  these screens are OLED they're made by  Samsung but this one is definitely a  step above and if you like watching  videos playing back HDR looks fantastic  on here especially in 1440p whereas the  1 + 7 Pro does not get as bright the  highlights are quite a bit dimmer and  it's a little bit more flat even in the  vivid mode so as far as watching videos  the note m+ is definitely a step above  now next we can go into the speakers and  if you're watching videos the speakers  are definitely better on the note 10  [Music]  both of them are usable but in certain  situations in the real world if you're  in a noisy environment say at a  restaurant if you're out somewhere with  friends and you're wanting to share a  funny video or something cool that you  found a lot of times with the 1 plus 7  throw it is just too quiet just like my  iPhone it's actually quieter than the  iPhones whereas the note 10 plus it has  the extra volume and that definitely  helps out in those certain situations  now the last thing that I want to talk  about and this is a huge one that is  cameras the note 10 plus is definitely a  huge step ahead in photo quality now the  1 plus 7 pro for the price is quite good  but it is inconsistent sometimes it's  overexposed underexposed to warm to cool  all those kind of things you can get  great photos but it is a lot more  limited and a lot more inconsistent  whereas Samsung has made some fantastic  improvements with photo quality it's  very consistent and they unlock certain  things like being able to do a panorama  with the standard or the wide angle or  being able to use night mode with either  the front-facing camera or any of the  three rear-facing cameras to get great  quality nighttime photos whereas with  the oneplus you can only use that  standard camera so there you guys have  it that is my real-world comparison  between the oneplus 7 pro 